{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Written on the Body", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Nine to Five: Don't Be So Sure!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understand actions, events, and experiences in present, past or future and in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect vs. Present Perfect Continuous", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect  and the Present Perfect Continuous tenses to talk about something that has recently finished and has an ongoing effect on a present situation. <br/>You use the Present Perfect to talk about the result of a past action in the present.<br/>You use the Present Perfect Continuous to talk about the ongoing process of a repeated past action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about your experiences. These could be at any unspecified time in your life. <br/><br/>For  example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> I have been to Europe. </span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> He has never tried sushi. </span><br/><br/> When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and its connection to the present, because you are referencing the event now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">Many professional athletes have become accustomed to hiding injuries.</span><br/> = Athletes still get injuries in the present.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The Present Perfect focuses on the result of a past action on the present situation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect Continuous to focus on the ongoing process of a repeated action. The result in the present situation is due to the ongoing process. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I've been using this new app on my phone to keep track of my time, and it's been saving me so much time!</span> = I still use the app, and it is a repeated, ongoing process.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>Look at some examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The work  of a professional athlete has never been considered a traditional nine-to-five job. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Recently, however, the job has been evolving into something more like a twenty-four seven commitment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "NFL quarterback Peyton Manning has become the poster boy for this modern workload. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Before most of his peers have eaten breakfast, Peyton has gone through an early workout, including stretching and core strengthening.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Impersonal Reports", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the Passive form to report events or situation in an impersonal way.<br/>You use verbs like <span class=\"italic\">suggest</span>, <span class=\"italic\">learn</span>, <span class=\"italic\">report</span>, <span class=\"italic\">say</span>, <span class=\"italic\">believe</span> or <span class=\"italic\">rumor</span> in the Passive form to write or talk about impersonal reports.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Passive form to report events in an impersonal way. The subject is not specific, but general.<br/>You can use verbs like <span class=\"italic\">suggest</span>, <span class=\"italic\">learn</span>, <span class=\"italic\">report</span>, <span class=\"italic\">say</span>, <span class=\"italic\">believe</span> or <span class=\"italic\">rumor</span> in the Passive form to write or talk about impersonal reports.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Structure:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">It</span>+ Passive form + <span class=\"italic\">that</span> ...<br/>Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">It is reported that</span> too much overtime may be bad for your health.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Subject + Passive form + <span class=\"italic\">to</span> ... <br/>Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">He is known to</span> be a very understanding manager.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<br/>Read the following examples from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "He is known to possess a tireless work ethic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "In fact, he is rumored to analyze more game tapes than most NFL coaches.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He is reported to possess an encyclopedic knowledge of defensive formations and tendencies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "After watching tape, he is said to spend a few hours on the field, practicing with his wide receivers.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nine-to-five", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a typical working day", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The work  of a professional athlete has never been considered a traditional nine-to-five job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about health and work.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "twenty-four seven", "type": "name"}, {"content": "all the time; twenty-four hours per day, seven days per week", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Recently, however, the job has been evolving into something more like a twenty-four seven commitment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tireless", "type": "name"}, {"content": "never resting or becoming tired", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is known to possess a tireless work ethic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "core", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the center of the body, including the abdominal and oblique muscles", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He strengthens his core every day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "peer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "friend or colleague", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Before most of his peers have eaten breakfast, Peyton has gone through an early workout, including stretching and core strengthening. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bumps and bruises", "type": "name"}, {"content": "small injuries", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If it's a Monday morning, he'll head over to the medical center, where he will receive treatment for the various bumps and bruises suffered in Sunday's game.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "split-second", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely fast", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All of this information comes in handy on game day, when he has to make numerous split-second decision.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le02ob10aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "On a blank piece of paper, write the days of the week.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask a partner about their weekly schedule.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Fill in each day of your chart with the amount of time they work and study.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a final tally at the end of the work summarizing how much your partner works and studies.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I create a weekly schedule.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I interview my partner about work habits.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I summarize the results.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn11le02ob10re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn11le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "", "time": "0"}, {"image": "engenn11le02ob10re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "The work  of a professional athlete has never been considered a traditional nine-to-five job. Recently, however, the job has been evolving into something more like a twenty-four seven commitment. NFL quarterback Peyton Manning has become the poster boy for this modern workload.", "time": "100"}, {"image": "engenn11le02ob10re2img02.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "He is known to possess a tireless work ethic. His day starts early. Before most of his peers have eaten breakfast, Peyton has gone through an early workout, including stretching and core strengthening. If it's a Monday morning, he'll head over to the medical center, where he will receive treatment for the various bumps and bruises suffered in Sunday's game. Then, he watches film from the game. In fact, he is rumored to analyze more game tapes than most NFL coaches. He has been studying defenses for over twenty years, and he is reported to possess an encyclopedic knowledge of defensive formations and tendencies. All of this information comes in handy on game day, when he has to make numerous split-second decision.", "time": "16000"}, {"image": "engenn11le02ob10re2img03.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "After watching tape, he is said to spend a few hours on the field, practicing with his wide receivers. Then it's off to the gym again for more conditioning. Once the physical half of his day is complete, the mental half begins. He meets with coaches to discuss new plays. He meets with sponsors to discuss new endorsements, and he takes care of his media commitments by giving interviews and doing photo shoots. On top of that, he still finds time for the fans, often signing autographs for hours at a time.\n<br/>\nWhen he gets home, it's late, but he doesn't let up. It is reported that while he's on the road, he'll often call a few of his wide receivers up to his room after 9:00 p.m., just to go over the plays one last time.", "time": "59000"}], "coverimg": "engenn11le02ob10re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "audio", "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about health and wellness.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about what I've been doing or what I've done. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can report statements.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "How many hours per week do you work or study? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What is an acceptable number of hours to work in a week?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "The work ethic of a champion.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": []}, {"id": 1, "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " The quarterback who won't <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">let up</span>.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct!", "atte